00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.919
- Hey, this is Vinny Testaverde, and I am here to build my squad.

00:00:07.882 --> 00:00:10.051
Now I'm gonna pick my all-time football lineup.

00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:12.178
OK, my first pick at quarterback is

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:14.139
Tom Brady.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.266
Well, I think Tom has proven himself.

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:18.435
He's one of the best, if not the best to ever do it.

00:00:19.394 --> 00:00:21.021
Put him in any situation, any weather,

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.940
playoffs, Super Bowl, whatever the situation, he can handle it.

00:00:24.274 --> 00:00:24.941
Running back.

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:26.693
Jim Brown.

00:00:27.152 --> 00:00:28.945
You can even ask the greatest of the great running backs.

00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:31.865
They'll all tell you Jim Brown was the best to ever play at his position.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.491
Wide receiver.

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:35.326
Have to go with Randy Moss.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.787
I would loved to have had Randy on my team to throw to.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:40.081
So, I'm gonna go with Deion Sanders because

00:00:40.081 --> 00:00:42.876
he was the best at it, and if you ask the fastest of the fast,

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.378
they would tell you that

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.047
they would never wanna play against Deion because

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.298
he can cover everybody.

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:50.300
And finally, linebackers.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.303
I'll go with Ray Lewis because not only was he great, but

00:00:53.303 --> 00:00:55.680
he's a former teammate of mine, and I love Ray.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:56.389
Great player.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:01:00.769
And if it wasn't him, it'd be Lawrence Taylor,

00:01:00.769 --> 00:01:02.937
but there's a lot of comparisons between the two, but

00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:05.065
Ray wins out because he was a teammate.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.399
Locked in.

00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:07.859
Quarterback, Tom Brady.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:09.861
One of the best to ever do it.

00:01:09.861 --> 00:01:11.696
Jim Brown at running back, the best to ever do it.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.782
We got Randy Moss, who

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:17.327
nobody can guard at any era.

00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:19.829
Deion Sanders, the fastest of them all.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.081
Can cover anybody.

00:01:21.164 --> 00:01:22.165
And finally, Ray Lewis.

00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:23.333
I think I picked a good squad.

